---
import SourcePanel from "./SourcePanel.astro";

const { topic, next, compact = false } = Astro.props;
const nextDescription = next?.slug === "cosmic-address"
  ? "Step back and see Yuga, Maha Yuga, Manvantara, Kalpa, and Brahma's lifespan as one complete map."
  : "Discover the great chapters that unfold within a Kalpa.";
const facts = [
  ["Duration", "4.32 billion human years"],
  ["Defined as", "Daytime of Brahma"],
  ["Contains", "1,000 Maha Yugas"],
  ["Current Kalpa", "Shveta Varaha Kalpa"],
];
const buildSteps = [
  ["Four Yugas", "Satya, Treta, Dvapara, Kali"],
  ["One Maha Yuga", "A complete four-age cycle"],
  ["71 Maha Yugas", "One Manvantara"],
  ["14 Manvantaras", "The major chapters of a Kalpa"],
  ["One Kalpa", "One daytime of Brahma"],
];
const cinemaPhases = [
  ["Sunrise", "Creation begins", "The cosmic day opens and manifestation starts."],
  ["Daylight", "Universe unfolds", "Manvantaras and Maha Yugas pass inside the Day of Brahma."],
  ["Sunset", "The day completes", "Creation moves toward rest as the cosmic evening arrives."],
  ["Night", "Brahma rests", "The universe becomes unmanifest before the next dawn."],
];
---

<article class="kalpa-reading">
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">Cosmic Clock Project � Kalpa</p>
    <h1>One Day That Lasts 4.32 Billion Years</h1>
    <p class="lead">What if a single day was so vast that mountains could rise, continents could shift, and entire civilizations could appear and disappear before sunset?</p>
  </header>

  <dl class="facts">
    {facts.map(([label, value]) => <div><dt>{label}</dt><dd>{value}</dd></div>)}
  </dl>

  <div class="reading-body">
    <main>
      <section>
        <h2>A day unlike any other</h2>
        <p>When someone says <strong>one day</strong>, we immediately think of 24 hours.</p>
        <p>It is the rhythm of our lives. We wake up. We work. We rest. Then another day begins.</p>
        <p>But Hindu cosmology invites us to imagine a completely different scale of time.</p>
        <p>According to traditional scriptures, there exists a day so immense that it spans <strong>4.32 billion human years</strong>.</p>
        <p>This extraordinary span of time is called a <strong>Kalpa</strong>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What is a Kalpa?</h2>
        <p>A Kalpa is one of the largest units of time described in Hindu cosmology.</p>
        <aside class="definition-card"><span>Traditional definition</span><strong>One daytime of Brahma</strong></aside>
        <p>According to the Puranic tradition, during this cosmic day, the universe unfolds through creation, preservation, and countless changes.</p>
        <p>When the day ends, the universe enters a period of rest known as the Night of Brahma, after which a new cosmic day begins.</p>
        <p>A Kalpa is therefore not the entire lifetime of the universe. It is one day in an ongoing cycle of cosmic time.</p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>

  <details class="full-guide" open={!compact} data-compact={compact || undefined}>
    <summary><span>Continue reading</span><b>Read full Kalpa guide</b></summary>
    <div class="reading-body">
      <main>
        <section>
          <h2>Building a Kalpa</h2>
          <p>By now, you have explored several layers of cosmic time. Each one builds upon the previous.</p>
          <p>Like small streams joining to form a great river, each cycle becomes part of a larger one.</p>
          <div class="build-ladder" aria-label="Kalpa structure">
            {buildSteps.map(([title, detail], index) => <article><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span><strong>{title}</strong><small>{detail}</small></article>)}
          </div>
          <p>This is the architecture of time described in Hindu cosmology. Every layer has its place. Every cycle contributes to something larger.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>How long is a Kalpa?</h2>
          <p>Traditional Hindu texts describe the calculation in a remarkably simple way.</p>
          <div class="calculation-card">
            <div><span>1 Kalpa contains</span><strong>1,000 Maha Yugas</strong></div>
            <div><span>1 Maha Yuga lasts</span><strong>4.32 million years</strong></div>
            <div class="result"><span>Therefore</span><strong>1 Kalpa = 4.32 billion human years</strong></div>
          </div>
          <p>This is the same astonishing number introduced at the beginning of the journey. Now, at last, you know where it comes from.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>A universe that breathes</h2>
          <p>One of the most beautiful ideas in Hindu cosmology is that the universe follows a rhythm.</p>
          <p>Not unlike breathing.</p>
          <p>During the Day of Brahma, creation unfolds. Worlds exist. Life evolves. Civilizations rise and fall.</p>
          <p>When evening arrives, the universe enters the Night of Brahma. Creation becomes unmanifest. The next cosmic day begins only after this immense night has passed.</p>
          <p>This recurring cycle of manifestation and rest gives Hindu cosmology its deeply cyclical character.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="kalpa-cinema" data-kalpa-cinema>
          <h2>A visual journey through a Kalpa</h2>
          <p>As you move through this section, the cosmic day travels from sunrise to daylight, then sunset, and finally into the star-filled Night of Brahma.</p>
          <div class="cinema-stage" aria-label="Scroll animated Kalpa timeline">
            <div class="cinema-sky" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
            <div class="cinema-sun" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="cinema-track">
              {cinemaPhases.map(([phase, title, detail], index) => <article><small>{phase}</small><strong>{title}</strong><p>{detail}</p><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span></article>)}
            </div>
            <div class="cinema-line" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></div>
          </div>
          <p>Without memorizing every number, the idea becomes visible: a Kalpa is the universe's day, followed by its night, in an endless rhythm described by Hindu cosmology.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Which Kalpa are we living in?</h2>
          <p>According to the traditional Puranic chronology, we are currently living in the <strong>Shveta Varaha Kalpa</strong>.</p>
          <p>This is the name traditionally given to the present Day of Brahma.</p>
          <aside class="note"><p class="eyebrow">Our current position</p><p><strong>Shveta Varaha Kalpa</strong> � <strong>7th Manvantara</strong> � <strong>28th Maha Yuga</strong> � <strong>Kali Yuga</strong></p></aside>
          <p>The cosmic timeline is remarkably detailed. It does not simply describe vast stretches of time. It also tells us where we stand within them.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Why is 4.32 billion interesting?</h2>
          <p>For many readers today, this number immediately stands out because modern science estimates the Earth to be about <strong>4.54 billion years old</strong>.</p>
          <p>It is tempting to compare these two figures. However, they come from very different frameworks.</p>
          <div class="comparison-panel">
            <article><span>Traditional cosmology</span><strong>4.32 billion years</strong><p>The duration of a Kalpa in the Puranic model.</p></article>
            <article><span>Modern science</span><strong>About 4.54 billion years</strong><p>The estimated age of Earth based on evidence such as radiometric dating and geological research.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p>The similarity in scale is often discussed, but the two numbers arise from different methods and should not be treated as direct equivalents.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Did you know?</h2>
          <p>A full day and night of Brahma lasts:</p>
          <div class="day-night-card">
            <div><span>Day</span><strong>4.32 billion years</strong></div>
            <b>+</b>
            <div><span>Night</span><strong>4.32 billion years</strong></div>
            <b>=</b>
            <div><span>Full cycle</span><strong>8.64 billion years</strong></div>
          </div>
          <p>And yet, this is still only one day in Brahma's life.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Pause and reflect</h2>
          <p>Imagine living for 100 years.</p>
          <p>Now compare that to 4.32 billion years.</p>
          <p>Your entire lifetime would be less than a blink within a Kalpa.</p>
          <p>Hindu cosmology invites us to step outside the scale of ordinary human history and consider time from a cosmic perspective.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>What comes next?</h2>
          <p>A Kalpa is only one day. But every day is followed by a night.</p>
          <p>What happens to the universe during that immense cosmic night?</p>
          <p>Does everything disappear? Or does creation simply rest until the next dawn?</p>
          <p>The next chapter explores one of the most fascinating ideas in Hindu cosmology: the <strong>Day and Night of Brahma</strong>.</p>
          <a class="recap-link" href="/atlas/cosmic-address"><span>Need the full map?</span><strong>Read: Where Are We in the Cosmic Timeline?</strong><small>See Yuga, Maha Yuga, Manvantara, Kalpa, Brahma's lifespan, and our current cosmic address together.</small></a>
        </section>
      </main>
    </div>

    <SourcePanel sources={topic.data.sources} sourceNote={topic.data.sourceNote} traditionNote={topic.data.traditionNote} reviewedBy={topic.data.reviewedBy} lastReviewed={topic.data.lastReviewed} contentVersion={topic.data.contentVersion} />
  </details>

  <a class="continue" href={`/atlas/${next?.slug ?? "manvantara"}`}>
    <span><small>Ready to move deeper?</small><strong>Next: {next?.title ?? "Manvantara"}</strong><em>{nextDescription}</em></span>
    <b>Explore next layer -></b>
  </a>
</article>

<style>
  .kalpa-reading { color:#eee3cf; }
  header,.reading-body,.facts,.kalpa-reading :global(.source-panel),.continue,.full-guide > summary { width:min(100% - 2rem,72rem); margin-inline:auto; }
  header { padding:clamp(3rem,7vw,7rem) 0 2.5rem; }
  header p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width:62ch; color:#b3aca1; line-height:1.85; }
  header strong,.reading-body strong { color:#e9b65f; font-weight:650; }
  h1,h2 { font-family:var(--serif); font-weight:400; letter-spacing:0; }
  h1 { max-width:15ch; margin:.35rem 0 1rem; font-size:clamp(3.2rem,6vw,6rem); line-height:1; }
  .lead { color:#d0c5b3 !important; font-size:clamp(1.08rem,1.5vw,1.3rem); }
  .facts { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); border-block:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.18); }
  .facts div { padding:1rem; }
  .facts div + div { border-left:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.14); }
  dt { color:#99938a; font-size:.62rem; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.1em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  dd { margin:.25rem 0 0; color:#e5dac8; font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.05rem; }
  .reading-body { padding-block:2rem; }
  main { width:min(100%,46rem); }
  section { border-bottom:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.14); padding-block:2rem; }
  h2 { margin:0 0 .8rem; font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.6rem); line-height:1.15; }
  section p,section li { color:#aaa49a; line-height:1.85; }
  section p { margin:.65rem 0 0; }
  .definition-card,.note,.calculation-card,.comparison-panel article,.day-night-card,.continue,.full-guide>summary { backdrop-filter:blur(14px); box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.025); }
  .definition-card { display:grid; gap:.35rem; margin:1.25rem 0; border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.2); border-radius:.9rem; padding:1rem; background:rgb(233 182 95/.045); }
  .definition-card span,.calculation-card span,.comparison-panel span,.day-night-card span { color:#a99f91; font-size:.62rem; font-weight:850; letter-spacing:.1em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .definition-card strong { color:#ffe3a1; font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.45rem; font-weight:500; }
  .build-ladder { display:grid; gap:.55rem; margin:1.35rem 0; }
  .build-ladder article { display:grid; grid-template-columns:3.25rem 1fr; gap:.2rem .85rem; border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.15); border-radius:.85rem; padding:.8rem .95rem; background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgb(233 182 95/.055),rgb(255 255 255/.018)); }
  .build-ladder span { grid-row:1/3; color:#e9b65f; font-size:.68rem; font-weight:900; letter-spacing:.12em; }
  .build-ladder strong { color:#f0e3cc; font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.15rem; }
  .build-ladder small { color:#9f978d; }
  .calculation-card { display:grid; gap:.7rem; margin:1.35rem 0; border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.18); border-radius:1rem; padding:1rem; background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgb(233 182 95/.06),rgb(255 255 255/.018)); }
  .calculation-card div { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:1rem; border-bottom:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.1); padding:.65rem 0; }
  .calculation-card div:last-child { border-bottom:0; }
  .calculation-card strong { text-align:right; }
  .calculation-card .result strong { color:#ffe3a1; font-size:1.1rem; }
  .kalpa-cinema { min-height: 185vh; }
  .cinema-stage { position: sticky; top: 1rem; min-height: min(72vh, 38rem); overflow: hidden; border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.18); border-radius:1.2rem; margin:1.35rem 0; background:#07131b; box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.04),0 20px 54px rgb(0 0 0/.22); }
  .cinema-sky { position:absolute; inset:0; background:linear-gradient(180deg,#f2b36e 0%,#28495f 48%,#07131b 100%); transition:background 120ms linear; }
  .cinema-sky span { position:absolute; inset:0; opacity:0; transition:opacity 120ms linear; }
  .cinema-sky span:nth-child(1) { background:linear-gradient(180deg,#86b8d5 0%,#1b4961 48%,#09202d 100%); opacity:clamp(0, calc((var(--kalpa-progress, 0) - .18) * 5), 1); }
  .cinema-sky span:nth-child(2) { background:linear-gradient(180deg,#9b5b46 0%,#251a2c 52%,#080b16 100%); opacity:clamp(0, calc((var(--kalpa-progress, 0) - .52) * 5), 1); }
  .cinema-sky span:nth-child(3) { background:radial-gradient(circle at 28% 22%,rgb(255 255 255/.7) 1px,transparent 2px),radial-gradient(circle at 72% 34%,rgb(255 255 255/.55) 1px,transparent 2px),radial-gradient(circle at 54% 72%,rgb(255 255 255/.45) 1px,transparent 2px),linear-gradient(180deg,#060816,#01040a); background-size:90px 90px,130px 130px,160px 160px,auto; opacity:clamp(0, calc((var(--kalpa-progress, 0) - .72) * 5), 1); }
  .cinema-sun { position:absolute; left:var(--kalpa-sun-left, 8%); top:var(--kalpa-sun-top, 70%); width:4.8rem; aspect-ratio:1; border-radius:50%; background:radial-gradient(circle,#fff5bc,#e9b65f 48%,rgb(233 182 95/.12) 70%,transparent 72%); box-shadow:0 0 60px rgb(233 182 95/.55); transform:translate(-50%,-50%); }
  .cinema-track { position:absolute; left:7%; right:7%; bottom:5.2rem; display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(14rem,1fr)); gap:1rem; transform:translateX(calc(var(--kalpa-progress, 0) * -18%)); transition:transform 120ms linear; }
  .cinema-track article { position:relative; min-height:10rem; border:1px solid rgb(255 255 255/.14); border-radius:1rem; padding:1rem; background:rgb(2 10 16/.58); backdrop-filter:blur(16px); box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.04); }
  .cinema-track small { color:#e9b65f; font-size:.62rem; font-weight:900; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .cinema-track strong { display:block; margin:.45rem 0; color:#fff0cf; font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.35rem; font-weight:500; }
  .cinema-track p { color:#cfc4b4; font-size:.82rem; line-height:1.55; }
  .cinema-track article > span { position:absolute; right:1rem; bottom:.8rem; color:rgb(233 182 95/.34); font-family:var(--serif); font-size:2rem; }
  .cinema-line { position:absolute; left:7%; right:7%; bottom:2.8rem; height:2px; background:rgb(255 255 255/.16); }
  .cinema-line i { display:block; width:calc(var(--kalpa-progress, 0) * 100%); height:100%; border-radius:999px; background:linear-gradient(90deg,#e9b65f,#65d7dc); box-shadow:0 0 18px rgb(233 182 95/.34); }
  .day-ribbon { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(7,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:.45rem; margin:1.35rem 0; }
  .day-ribbon article { min-height:6.2rem; border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.15); border-radius:.85rem; padding:.7rem; background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgb(233 182 95/.07),rgb(255 255 255/.018)); }
  .day-ribbon .night { border-color:rgb(101 215 220/.24); background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgb(101 215 220/.08),rgb(255 255 255/.018)); }
  .day-ribbon span { color:#e9b65f; font-size:.62rem; font-weight:900; }
  .day-ribbon strong { display:block; margin-top:2rem; color:#f0e3cc; font-size:.78rem; line-height:1.25; }
  .note { margin:1.5rem 0 0; border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.17); border-left:2px solid #e9b65f; border-radius:.7rem; padding:.8rem 1rem; background:rgb(233 182 95/.035); }
  .note p { margin:.25rem 0; color:#c2b9aa; }
  .comparison-panel { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:.7rem; margin:1.35rem 0; }
  .comparison-panel article { border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.15); border-radius:.85rem; padding:1rem; background:rgb(255 255 255/.02); }
  .comparison-panel strong { display:block; margin:.45rem 0; color:#ffe3a1; font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.25rem; }
  .day-night-card { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; gap:.65rem; align-items:center; margin:1.35rem 0; border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.18); border-radius:1rem; padding:1rem; background:rgb(255 255 255/.02); }
  .day-night-card div { display:grid; gap:.35rem; }
  .day-night-card b { color:#e9b65f; font-size:1.2rem; }
  .day-night-card strong { color:#ffe3a1; font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.05rem; }
  .recap-link { display:grid; gap:.28rem; margin-top:1.35rem; border:1px solid rgb(101 215 220/.24); border-radius:.95rem; padding:1rem 1.1rem; background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgb(101 215 220/.08),rgb(255 255 255/.02)); color:#65d7dc; box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.035); }
  .recap-link span { color:#a99f91; font-size:.62rem; font-weight:850; letter-spacing:.1em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .recap-link strong { color:#dfffff; font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.3rem; font-weight:500; }
  .recap-link small { color:#aaa49a; line-height:1.55; }
  .full-guide { border:0; }
  .full-guide:not([data-compact]) > summary { display:none; }
  .full-guide > summary { display:flex; width:fit-content; align-items:center; gap:.55rem; margin-top:.9rem; border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.24); border-radius:999px; padding:.55rem .8rem; background:rgb(233 182 95/.035); color:#e9b65f; cursor:pointer; list-style:none; }
  .full-guide > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display:none; }
  .full-guide > summary span { color:#99938a; font-size:.62rem; letter-spacing:.08em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .full-guide > summary b { font-size:.67rem; }
  .full-guide[open] > summary b { font-size:0; }
  .full-guide[open] > summary b::after { font-size:.67rem; content:"Hide full guide"; }
  .full-guide[open] > .reading-body { animation:guide-reveal 420ms ease both; }
  .continue { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:1rem; margin-top:2rem; border:1px solid rgb(101 215 220/.22); border-radius:1rem; padding:1.2rem 1.35rem; background:linear-gradient(100deg,rgb(101 215 220/.055),transparent); color:#65d7dc; }
  .continue span > * { display:block; }
  .continue small { color:#99938a; font-size:.62rem; letter-spacing:.1em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .continue strong { font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.7rem; font-weight:400; }
  .continue em { color:#aaa49a; font-size:.72rem; font-style:normal; }
  .continue b { font-size:.68rem; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .kalpa-reading{border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.2);border-radius:1.4rem;padding-bottom:1rem;background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgb(10 27 36/.72),rgb(3 13 20/.48));box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.035),0 24px 80px rgb(0 0 0/.22);backdrop-filter:blur(20px) saturate(115%)}
  .facts{overflow:hidden;border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.18);border-radius:1rem;background:rgb(255 255 255/.025);box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.025);backdrop-filter:blur(14px)}
  @keyframes guide-reveal { from { opacity:0; transform:translateY(-8px) } to { opacity:1; transform:none } }
  @media(max-width:900px){ .cinema-stage{min-height:34rem}.cinema-track{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(12rem,1fr));left:1rem;right:auto;width:max-content;transform:translateX(calc(var(--kalpa-progress, 0) * -42%));}.day-ribbon{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));} .comparison-panel{grid-template-columns:1fr;} .day-night-card{grid-template-columns:1fr;} .day-night-card b{display:none;} }
  @media(max-width:800px){ .facts{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.facts div:nth-child(odd){border-left:0}.facts div:nth-child(n+3){border-top:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.14)} .continue{align-items:flex-end} }
  @media(max-width:620px){ .day-ribbon{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;} .continue{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column;} }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  // @ts-nocheck
  const kalpaCinemas = document.querySelectorAll("[data-kalpa-cinema]");
  const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
  const clamp = (value, min, max) => Math.min(max, Math.max(min, value));
  let ticking = false;

  function updateKalpaCinema() {
    kalpaCinemas.forEach((section) => {
      if (reduceMotion) {
        section.style.setProperty("--kalpa-progress", "0.45");
        section.style.setProperty("--kalpa-sun-left", "43%");
        section.style.setProperty("--kalpa-sun-top", "24%");
        return;
      }
      const rect = section.getBoundingClientRect();
      const travel = Math.max(1, rect.height - window.innerHeight);
      const progress = clamp((window.innerHeight * 0.12 - rect.top) / travel, 0, 1);
      section.style.setProperty("--kalpa-progress", progress.toFixed(4));
      section.style.setProperty("--kalpa-sun-left", `${8 + progress * 78}%`);
      section.style.setProperty("--kalpa-sun-top", `${70 - Math.sin(progress * Math.PI) * 46}%`);
    });
    ticking = false;
  }

  function requestKalpaCinemaUpdate() {
    if (!ticking) {
      ticking = true;
      window.requestAnimationFrame(updateKalpaCinema);
    }
  }

  updateKalpaCinema();
  window.addEventListener("scroll", requestKalpaCinemaUpdate, { passive: true });
  window.addEventListener("resize", requestKalpaCinemaUpdate);
</script>